<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles III of Naples</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1345–1386</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Charles II of Hungary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> (1345–1386), known as Charles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durazzo</a>, was a member of the Angevin dynasty. With Hungarian support and the backing of Pope Urban VI he overthrew his cousin Joanna I in 1381 and became king of Naples, and she was killed in 1382. In 1385 he also seized the Hungarian throne, but he was attacked at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a> in February 1386 and died of his wounds.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-naples.jpg" alt="Charles III of Naples" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_II,_Chronicon_Pictum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
